direction: right

title: |md
  ## Argument access by program type
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

fentry: "fentry/fexit" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("fentry/vfs_read")
    int BPF_PROG(p, struct file *f,
                 char *buf, size_t n,
                 loff_t *pos) { ... }
    ```
    **Does:** trampoline supplies BTF-typed
    function args.

    **State:** `f` is trusted `PTR_TO_BTF_ID`,
    so direct field reads are allowed.
  |
}

kprobe: "kprobe/kretprobe" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("kprobe/vfs_read")
    int BPF_KPROBE(p, struct file *f, ...) { ... }
    ```
    **Does:** trap saves CPU registers in
    `struct pt_regs`.

    **State:** extracted pointers are scalars;
    use `bpf_probe_read_kernel` for fields.
  |
}

tracepoint: "tracepoint/..." {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("tracepoint/syscalls/sys_enter_read")
    int p(struct trace_event_raw_sys_enter *ctx)
    ```
    **Does:** reads a copied event struct.

    **State:** stable fields from
    `/sys/kernel/tracing/events/.../format`,
    not live kernel objects.
  |
}

rawtp: "raw_tracepoint/..." {
  style.fill: "#fde68a"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("raw_tracepoint/sched_switch")
    int p(struct bpf_raw_tracepoint_args *ctx)
    ```
    **Does:** exposes raw tracepoint args as
    positional `u64` slots.

    **State:** lower-level than tracepoint;
    caller must unpack by index.
  |
}

tpbtf: "tp_btf/..." {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("tp_btf/sched_switch")
    int BPF_PROG(p, bool preempt,
                 struct task_struct *prev,
                 struct task_struct *next)
    ```
    **Does:** uses tracepoint BTF prototype.

    **State:** live typed pointers for the
    duration of the callback.
  |
}

fentry -> kprobe: "same target can be observed through older trap path"
kprobe -> tracepoint: "explicit events avoid fragile function names"
tracepoint -> rawtp: "skip copied struct when raw args are desired"
rawtp -> tpbtf: "BTF restores typed arguments for new code"
